OL,3,GNEWSAUK falls silent to mark Armistice
OL,4,ADay
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe UK has fallen silent to mark
OL,7,FArmistice Day, commemorating the end of
OL,8,FWorld War One.
OL,10,FThe two-minute silence took place to
OL,11,Fmark the end of the war and to remember
OL,12,Fthose who have died in conflicts.
OL,14,FCeremonies took place at the Cenotaph
OL,15,Fin London, the National Memorial
OL,16,FArboretum in Staffordshire, and across
OL,17,Fthe UK.
OL,19,FDefence Secretary Wes Streeting laid a
OL,20,Fwreath at the Cenotaph memorial, which
OL,21,Fwas also attended by senior military
OL,22,Ffigures, schoolchildren and cadets.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
